      "summary": "The setting moves from urgent shelter-seeking through a conditional oath of innocence to an appeal for public judgment. Confidence in God's protection leads into weapon imagery, then images of wrongdoing returning upon its maker, and finally a commitment to thanksgiving. Short phrases and contractions modernize the voice while retaining the lion, hands, dust, hearts and kidneys, shield, weapons, childbirth, pit, and head imagery. Interpretive choices include the rescue reading in verse 5, righteousness expressed as conduct in verse 9, and an added heat metaphor in verse 12. The closing praise does not report that rescue has already occurred.",
